problems.problem:
We call a quadruple $(a, b, c, d)$ of positive integers with $a \leq b \leq c \leq d$ good if we can colour each integer red, blue, green or purple such that

• of any $a$ consecutive integers at least one is red;
• of any $b$ consecutive integers at least one is blue;
• of any $c$ consecutive integers at least one is green;
• of any $d$ consecutive integers at least one is purple.

Determine all good quadruples with $a = 2$.
